<title>BELGIUM: EU to ease German pig movement ban.</title>
<headline>EU to ease German pig movement ban.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's Standing Veterinary Committee supported on Wednesday a further easing of movement restrictions on pigs in Germany, a European Commission official said.</p>
<p>Restrictions were imposed in February on pig movements in five German states and two districts in a sixth following outbreaks of swine fever. They were initially eased in March.</p>
<p>&quot;The committee has agreed to reduce the number of veterinary areas which are under restriction for domestic pigs,&quot; the official said, adding further details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>The ban on Dutch pig trade is unchanged, the official added.</p>
</text>
